cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use APAURA in your research, please cite it using the following information."
title: "APAURA: Alternative Polyadenylation Architecture, Usage, and Regulatory Analysis"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Boateng-Sarfo"
    given-names: "George"
version: "0.10.1"
date-released: "2026-09-23"
abstract: >
  APAURA is a Java toolkit for alternative polyadenylation analysis. It identifies
  poly(A) sites, quantifies poly(A)-site usage, characterizes TUTR and ALE architecture,
  detects intronic polyadenylation changes, and prioritizes candidate RNA-binding
  regulators associated with regulated regions.
